course: dictionary
lesson: 12562
title: Diameter: how wide a round thing is
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A diameter is a straight line that goes from one side of a circle to the other, passing right through the middle. «The pizza has a diameter of 30 centimetres» means that if you measured straight across the pizza through its centre, the distance would be 30 centimetres.
explain: Diameter also means the length of that line, so it tells you how wide a round thing is. «The water pipe has a small diameter, so only a little water can flow through it.» A pipe with a small diameter is narrow, and a pipe with a large diameter is wide.
explain: In maths, the diameter is twice the radius. The radius goes from the centre to the edge, so if a circle's radius is 5 centimetres, its diameter is 10 centimetres. Try it with a coin: lay a ruler across the middle, edge to edge, and that is the diameter.
fact: Diameter means a straight line from one side of a circle to the other, through the centre.
fact: Diameter also means how wide a circle or round thing is.
fact: «The wheel has a diameter of 60 centimetres.» means the wheel is 60 centimetres wide, measured through the centre.
fact: The diameter is twice the radius, so the radius is half the diameter.
fact: The circumference is about 3.14 times the diameter; 3.14 is called pi.
fact: «The planet is about 12,700 kilometres in diameter.» tells you how wide the whole planet is.
exercise: «The pizza has a diameter of 30 centimetres.» What does diameter mean here? | How thick the cheese is | *How wide the pizza is, edge to edge through the middle | How heavy the pizza is | How many slices it has
exercise: What is the straight line from one side of a circle to the other, through the centre, called? | Radius | Pi | Edge | *Diameter
exercise: A circle has a radius of 5 centimetres. What is its diameter? | 2 centimetres | *10 centimetres | 15 centimetres | 5 centimetres
test: «The wheel has a diameter of 60 centimetres.» Is the diameter measured from the centre to the edge, or from edge to edge through the centre? | *Edge to edge, through the centre | The thickness of the tyre | Distance from the centre to the edge | The distance all the way around the wheel
test: The diameter of a circle is 8 centimetres. What is its radius? | 16 centimetres | *4 centimetres | 8 centimetres | 2 centimetres
exam: Roughly how is the circumference of a circle related to its diameter? | *About 3.14 times the diameter | Half the diameter | Ten times the diameter | Exactly the same length as the diameter
